# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ethixweb India — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit .env.local.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. DATABASE — any Postgres (Supabase / Neon / Vercel Postgres / local)
#    Supabase:  Project Settings → Database → Connection string → "Transaction pooler"
#    Neon:      Dashboard → Connection details → pooled connection string
#    Local:     postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/ethixweb_india
#    Leave blank to fall back to a local JSON dev store (NOT for production).
#
#    PLACEHOLDER ON PURPOSE — no real credential of any kind belongs in a
#    committed file, not even a throwaway local one.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/ethixweb_india"

# Set to true when pointing at Supabase/Neon in production so the driver
# uses SSL and prepared-statement-safe pooling.
DATABASE_SSL="false"

# 2. ADMIN AUTH — the /admin dashboard is protected by these
ADMIN_EMAIL="admin@ethixweb.in"
#
# NOTE: the password below is the PUBLIC DEMO credential for this submission.
# It is committed on purpose so reviewers can log in — but that also means it
# is worthless as a secret. Change it before this site handles real leads.
# Minimum 12 characters. Use a unique password per environment.
ADMIN_PASSWORD="Ethixweb@India2026"
#
# Signing secret for the admin session cookie AND for the form's anti-bot
# timestamp. Generate a fresh one per environment with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET="REPLACE_ME_generate_with_the_command_above"

# 3. SITE
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# 4. OPTIONAL — spam protection
# Server-side IP rate limiting is on by default (in-memory). To also enable
# Cloudflare Turnstile, set both values and the widget appears automatically.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=""
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=""
